					<p>When choosing the fish that will be our pets, we must take into account some issues. Here are some tips when buying fish aquarium in Arkansas. Having an acrylic aquarium or a well-designed aquarium display is a source of relaxation, something that beautifies any home and does not require great care. That is why many people choose fish as pets.</p>
<p><strong>Which aquarium for homes to choose to start with</strong></p>
<p>Buying an aquarium with a bubble wall for children does not require allocating a considerable budget. As a first step, and as long as it isn&#8217;t crowded, a small, inexpensive aquarium in the wall will do the trick. But beware, cheap aquarium bubble walls do not mean uncomfortable or dangerous for the animal. The aquarium air curtain bubble wall without a filtration system should be forbidden. Also, look for an aquarium bubble wall air stone tube. There are complete acrylic aquarium kits that include all the necessary items to start an aquarium at very affordable prices.</p>
<p>Our tip feel free to come and see our different models of aquariums and aquarium fountains online! Our consultants are at your disposal to help you choose your size or the aquarium display necessary for your maintenance.</p>
<p><strong>What should be the volume of the aquarium for home</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>To start with, for example, ten brilliant guppies, a 60 l aquarium can do the trick.</li>
<li>For a single goldfish, a Nano aquarium of 30 liters or less will be adequate. It will need to be changed to keep up with the evolution of goldfish.</li>
<li>Finally, do not forget to provide enough volume to install the aquarium accessories available in stock in stores while leaving enough space for the fish to move.</li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Tip:</strong> watch out for reproductions! If you do not want it, please specify that you only want females or males when purchasing your fish. On the other hand, logically plan a water volume accordingly if you want to witness the miracle of life in your aquarium.</p>
<p><strong>How to choose an aquarium display for children</strong></p>
<p>The development of an aquarium display is an exciting project. Whether your outdoor space is large or small, it is good to start by defining a style or an atmosphere, which will give unity to the decoration and inspire the choice of all other elements: acrylic aquarium materials, equipment, decorative objects, plants, flower pots. If you want to embark on this beautiful project for the summer, here are all our tips and decorating ideas for an aquarium fountains!</p>
<p><strong>What fish for an acrylic aquarium</strong></p>
<p>Among the hardiest fish and therefore the easiest to keep, we find, of course, the unmistakable goldfish that always makes children and adults dream. In terms of maintenance, it will require that half of your water be changed every two weeks and that the filtration system is cleaned once a month or even more if necessary.</p>
<p>But for a more colorful show, guppies and platys are great options. With their small size and the little waste they produce, it is possible to select several specimens that will live together in a relatively small space. Also, for them, the filtration system of the aquarium fountains must be cleaned every month. Only a quarter of the water needs to be changed every two weeks.</p>
<p><strong>Where to install your aquarium display</strong></p>
<p>Your child will want to set up the aquarium display in his room. A solution that is still entirely possible on the condition that certain requirements are met:</p>
<p><strong>The aquarium display needs solid, stable, and level support:</strong> it must be placed on a piece of furniture that can support its weight (a 60 l aquarium can weigh up to 75 kg when filled with water and equipped with accessories) and which is not condemned to move. Forget about the dresser top with endless drawer openings, and of course, don&#8217;t imagine putting your aquarium on a wall shelf.</p>
<p><strong>The aquarium display should not receive direct sunlight</strong>: direct UV rays will raise the temperature of the water and create thermal differences between day and night. Also, excessive heat (light) will promote algae growth. For the same reasons, the aquarium should not be placed near a heat source, such as a radiator.</p>
<p><strong>The aquarium must be close to an electrical outlet</strong>: it is essential for operating the filter pump.If you can&#8217;t find the perfect place to put the aquarium in your room, let your child choose the right location for him in the living room or elsewhere.</p>
